1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Every day, good food is discarded
while nearby communities still need meals.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
MealSaver closes that gap by turning surplus food
into a fast, accountable rescue workflow.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:19,500
Food businesses post extra food, verified NGOs
discover compatible pickups nearby,

4
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:27,000
and both sides track the handover through one platform.
The goal is simple: rescue more, waste less.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,500
Let's start as a donor.

6
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:39,000
The dashboard summarizes active donations,
completed deliveries, meals saved, and food waste reduced.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Creating a listing captures food type, condition,
quantity, expiry, contact details, and pickup location.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:55,500
Cooked food with a short shelf life
is marked urgent automatically.

9
00:00:55,500 --> 00:01:05,000
Once submitted, MealSaver starts matching in the background
instead of waiting for manual coordination.

10
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:11,500
On the NGO side, nearby donations
are organized by urgency and distance.

11
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:18,500
Teams can search, filter, review pickup windows,
and accept a suitable donation.

12
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:26,000
Eligibility checks cover verification, food preferences,
service area, and capacity.

13
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Acceptance creates a tracked pickup assignment
with the donor address, contact information, timing, and status.

14
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:43,000
This gives the NGO a clear operational checklist
instead of fragmented calls and messages.

15
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:50,500
At collection, the handover is protected
by a six-digit OTP and a visual safety checklist.

16
00:01:50,500 --> 00:02:03,000
The OTP ensures that the correct NGO receives the correct donation,
while the checklist keeps accountability part of the workflow.

17
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:08,000
For exceptional cases, admins have oversight.

18
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:14,000
They can verify organizations, monitor donation status,
and manually assign urgent pickups.

19
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:20,000
They can intervene as food approaches expiry.
Automation handles the common path; people resolve edge cases.

20
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Under the hood, a PostGIS query filters verified NGOs
by distance, category compatibility, and capacity,

21
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:39,000
then sorts nearest first. Completed deliveries generate impact records,
so operational actions become measurable outcomes.

22
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:48,000
The impact dashboard brings that together:
meals saved, kilograms rescued, and carbon impact avoided,

23
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:56,000
people served, and completed donation history.
Each number is tied to a real delivery record.

24
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:00,000
MealSaver: rescue surplus food, feed more people,
and make every handover count.